+Batch mode (patches/0180, GLM53_TF_BATCH > 1 with GLM53_TF_BATCH_SESSIONS=1): one store behind every batch slot.
+The index, the budget and the page slabs are shared; each slot has its own live caches, so the store keeps one
+``live`` map per slot (``bind_slots``) and every save / restore / ``begin`` runs on one slot (``on(slot)``). A
+restore COPIES an entry into the slot's caches, so a slot never reads the slabs afterwards: evicting an entry (or a
+page) while a slot runs the session it restored cannot touch that slot. The snapshot objects are plain copies
+(KDA states, conv windows, pending rows, drafter window) and restore into any slot of the same shapes. Requests
+admitted together cannot see each other's entries (none is stored yet), so rank 0 also counts a prefix shared with
+a prompt in flight (running or admitted in the same round) as a fork point (``plan(others=...)``): N sessions over
+one system prompt submitted at once still leave a fork mark for the next one.
